# The Clax app (Flutter). Its kit and home app are web files the browser
# tests also load (web/e2e/home-app.spec.ts, lockdown.spec.ts, map.spec.ts),
# as js_library targets so rules_js copies them beside the tests.

load("@aspect_rules_js//js:defs.bzl", "js_library")
load("@rules_apple//apple:versioning.bzl", "apple_bundle_version")
load("@rules_dart//dart:defs.bzl", "dart_analysis_config", "dart_analysis_options", "dart_analysis_test", "dart_binary", "dart_library")
load("@rules_flutter//flutter:defs.bzl", "flutter_application", "flutter_library", "flutter_test")
load("@rules_flutter//flutter:macos.bzl", "flutter_macos_app")
load("@rules_shell//shell:sh_binary.bzl", "sh_binary")
load("@rules_shell//shell:sh_test.bzl", "sh_test")
load("//bazel/flutter:android.bzl", "flutter_fat_apk")
load("//bazel/flutter:macos.bzl", "debug_app", "integration_main", "macos_helper")
load("//bazel/flutter:tests.bzl", "flutter_test_suite")

js_library(
    name = "kit",
    srcs = glob(
        ["assets/kit/**"],
        exclude = ["**/.qual"],
    ),
    visibility = ["//web:__pkg__"],
)

js_library(
    name = "home",
    srcs = glob(
        ["home/**"],
        exclude = ["**/.qual"],
    ),
    visibility = ["//web:__pkg__"],
)

js_library(
    name = "home_unit",
    srcs = glob(
        ["home_unit/**"],
        exclude = ["**/.qual"],
    ),
    visibility = ["//web:__pkg__"],
)
exports_files(["pubspec.lock"])

# `flutter analyze`'s rules for the app's Dart targets (the dart_analyze
# aspect .bazelrc applies to every test run).
dart_analysis_options(
    name = "analysis_options",
    src = "analysis_options.yaml",
    deps = ["@clax_app_pub//:flutter_lints"],
)

dart_analysis_config(
    name = "analysis_config",
    options = [":analysis_options"],
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)

flutter_library(
    name = "clax_app",
    package_name = "clax_app",
    srcs = glob(["lib/**/*.dart"]),
    tags = ["no-dart-format"],
    deps = [
        "@clax_app_pub//:archive",
        "@clax_app_pub//:cryptography",
        "@clax_app_pub//:file_picker",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_local_notifications",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_secure_storage",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_svg",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_timezone",
        "@clax_app_pub//:geolocator",
        "@clax_app_pub//:image_picker",
        "@clax_app_pub//:path_provider",
        "@clax_app_pub//:share_plus",
        "@clax_app_pub//:speech_to_text",
        "@clax_app_pub//:timezone",
        "@clax_app_pub//:webview_flutter",
        "@clax_app_pub//:xml",
    ],
)

# The app's unit and widget tests (`flutter test`), a test target per file,
# //apps/clax_app:<dir>_<file>, each run in a flutter_tester of its own and
# compiled with the other files of its directory (bazel/flutter/tests.bzl
# says why), against the app's sources and the files its tests read. The
# *_real_test.dart files, which run the real daemon, form a suite of their
# own with the warmed debug clax.
TEST_SUPPORT = glob(
    [
        "test/**/*.dart",
        "tool/**/*.dart",
    ],
    exclude = ["test/**/*_test.dart"],
) + [
    # Test files other tests import for their fakes.
    "test/platform/background_work_test.dart",
    "test/platform/device/device_host_test.dart",
    "test/ui/build_view_test.dart",
    "test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart",
    # The integration rig's pure helpers, which a unit test runs.
    "integration_test/newer.dart",
]

TEST_DATA = glob(
    [
        "assets/**",
        "home/**",
        "test/fixtures/**",
        "tool/eval/prompts.json",
    ],
    exclude = ["**/.qual"],
) + [
    "pubspec.yaml",
    "//web:contract_files",
]

REAL_TESTS = glob(["test/**/*_real_test.dart"])

# {suite: its test files}: a directory's, the top level's, and the real ones.
SUITES = {
    "real": REAL_TESTS,
    "root": glob(
        ["test/*_test.dart"],
        exclude = REAL_TESTS,
    ),
} | {
    d: glob(
        ["test/%s/**/*_test.dart" % d],
        exclude = REAL_TESTS,
    )
    for d in [
        "agent",
        "bundle",
        "clax",
        "daemon",
        "eval",
        "home",
        "platform",
        "ui",
    ]
}

[flutter_test_suite(
    name = "tests_%s" % suite,
    size = "medium",
    package_name = "clax_app",
    srcs = TEST_SUPPORT,
    assets = glob(
        [
            "assets/home/**",
            "assets/kit/**",
            "assets/prompt/**",
        ],
        exclude = ["**/.qual"],
    ),
    data = TEST_DATA + ([
        "//crates/clax-cli:clax",
        "//crates/clax-cli:clax_warm",
    ] if suite == "real" else []),
    # APP_NAME, as `flutter test` sets it beside UNIT_TEST_ASSETS
    # (flutter_test_suite): flutter_test then reads an asset from disk at
    # once, where through the engine the read would not finish within a
    # test's fake time.
    env = {"APP_NAME": "clax_app"} | ({"CLAX_TEST_BIN": "crates/clax-cli/clax"} if suite == "real" else {}),
    names = {t: t[len("test/"):-len(".dart")].replace("/", "_") for t in files},
    tests = files,
    deps = [
        ":clax_app",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_test",
    ],
) for suite, files in SUITES.items() if files]

# A test file in no suite would never run.
[fail("%s is in no suite of SUITES (apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel): add its directory" % t) for t in glob(["test/**/*_test.dart"]) if not [s for s in SUITES.values() if t in s]]

# `flutter analyze` (analysis_options.yaml) over the app's Dart: its
# library, and its tests, integration tests and tools as a library of their
# own, which nothing compiles but the analysis. No format check: the app's
# code is not `dart format`ted.
flutter_library(
    name = "checked_sources",
    package_name = "clax_app",
    srcs = glob([
        "integration_test/*.dart",
        "test/**/*.dart",
        "tool/**/*.dart",
    ]),
    tags = [
        "manual",
        "no-dart-format",
    ],
    deps = [
        ":clax_app",
        "@clax_app_pub//:archive",
        "@clax_app_pub//:cryptography",
        "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_test",
        "@clax_app_pub//:integration_test",
        "@clax_app_pub//:xml",
    ],
)

dart_analysis_test(
    name = "dart_analyze",
    targets = [
        ":checked_sources",
        ":clax_app",
    ],
)

# The prompt's copies of the contract match it (scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh).
sh_test(
    name = "prompt_sync",
    srcs = ["//scripts:sync-app-prompt.sh"],
    args = ["--check"],
    data = glob(["assets/prompt/**"]) + [
        "//docs:contract",
        "//web:contract_files",
    ],
)

# pubspec.yaml's assets: the files directly in each directory it names, as
# Flutter bundles them.
APP_ASSETS = glob(
    [
        "assets/home/*",
        "assets/kit/*",
        "assets/prompt/*",
    ],
    exclude = ["**/.qual"],
)

flutter_application(
    name = "app",
    package_name = "clax_app",
    srcs = glob(["lib/**/*.dart"]),
    assets = APP_ASSETS,
    main = "lib/main.dart",
    deps = [
        ":clax_app",
        "@rules_flutter//flutter:material_icons",
    ],
)

# pubspec.yaml's `version: <name>+<code>`.
VERSION_NAME = "1.0.0"

VERSION_CODE = "1"

sh_test(
    name = "version_sync",
    srcs = ["tool/version-sync.sh"],
    args = [
        VERSION_NAME,
        VERSION_CODE,
    ],
    data = ["pubspec.yaml"],
)

# The release APK, for both Android CPUs the app ships, with the embedded
# clax for each (bazel/flutter/android.bzl).
flutter_fat_apk(
    name = "apk",
    application = ":app",
    debug_key = "@android_debug_keystore//:key",
    kotlin_srcs = glob(["android/app/src/main/kotlin/**/*.kt"]),
    manifest = "android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml",
    # As android/app/build.gradle.kts gives them: minSdk 29, Flutter's
    # target SDK, and pubspec.yaml's version (:version_sync checks it).
    manifest_values = {
        "minSdkVersion": "29",
        "targetSdkVersion": "36",
        "versionCode": VERSION_CODE,
        "versionName": VERSION_NAME,
    },
    namespace = "dev.empathic.clax_app",
    native_files = {
        "//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_arm64": "arm64-v8a/libclax.so",
        "//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_x86_64": "x86_64/libclax.so",
    },
    package_name = "dev.empathic.clax",
    # Shrunk with R8 as Gradle's release build is: AGP's optimized defaults
    # and Flutter's rules; each plugin's and library's own rules come with it.
    proguard_specs = [
        "//bazel/android:proguard-android-optimize.txt",
        "//bazel/flutter:flutter_proguard_rules.pro",
    ],
    pub_hub_name = "clax_app_pub",
    resources = glob(["android/app/src/main/res/**"]),
    shrink_resources = 1,
    tags = ["no-remote"],
)

# The APK has what the Gradle build gives it (tool/apk-check.sh).
sh_test(
    name = "apk_test",
    srcs = ["tool/apk-check.sh"],
    args = [
        "$(rootpath :apk)",
        "$(rootpath @androidsdk//:aapt2)",
        "$(rootpath @androidsdk//:apksigner)",
    ],
    data = [
        ":apk",
        "@androidsdk//:aapt2",
        "@androidsdk//:apksigner",
    ],
    env = {
        "VERSION_CODE": VERSION_CODE,
        "VERSION_NAME": VERSION_NAME,
    },
    tags = ["no-remote"],
)

# The macOS app, with the optimized host clax in its Resources, where the
# app's supervisor starts it (lib/daemon/supervisor.dart), signed as a
# sandboxed helper (bazel/flutter/macos.bzl).
macos_helper(
    name = "macos_clax",
    binary = "//crates/clax-cli:clax_opt",
    # A debug app is not sandboxed: its helper is signed without them.
    entitlements = select({
        ":dbg": None,
        "//conditions:default": "macos/Runner/ClaxHelper.entitlements",
    }),
)

config_setting(
    name = "dbg",
    values = {"compilation_mode": "dbg"},
)

# pubspec.yaml's version, as Flutter's Xcode build gives it to the bundle.
apple_bundle_version(
    name = "macos_version",
    build_version = VERSION_CODE,
    short_version_string = VERSION_NAME,
)

flutter_macos_app(
    name = "macos_app",
    additional_contents = {":macos_clax": "Resources"},
    # The Xcode build's PRODUCT_NAME (macos/Runner/Configs/AppInfo.xcconfig).
    app_name = "clax_app",
    application = ":app",
    bundle_id = "dev.empathic.clax",
    version = ":macos_version",
)

# The macOS app has what the Xcode build gives it (tool/macos-app-check.sh).
sh_test(
    name = "macos_app_test",
    srcs = ["tool/macos-app-check.sh"],
    args = ["$(rootpath :macos_app)"],
    data = [":macos_app"],
    env = {
        "VERSION_CODE": VERSION_CODE,
        "VERSION_NAME": VERSION_NAME,
    },
    tags = ["no-remote"],
    target_compatible_with = ["@platforms//os:macos"],
)

# The home app's bundle (assets/home/home.clax and release.json), packed
# from home/ by tool/pack_home.dart, which needs only the bundle format and
# no Flutter. `bazelisk run //apps/clax_app:home_bundle` (just home-bundle)
# writes them into the checkout; the key is read from outside it
# (scripts/build-home-bundle.sh), so this is a run target, never cached.
dart_library(
    name = "bundle_format",
    package_name = "clax_app",
    srcs = [
        "lib/agent/icon_svg.dart",
        "lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart",
        "lib/bundle/bundle_writer.dart",
        "lib/bundle/content_hash.dart",
        "lib/bundle/manifest.dart",
        "lib/bundle/signing.dart",
    ],
    deps = [
        "@clax_app_pub//:archive",
        "@clax_app_pub//:cryptography",
        "@clax_app_pub//:xml",
    ],
)

dart_binary(
    name = "pack_home",
    main = "tool/pack_home.dart",
    deps = [":bundle_format"],
)

sh_binary(
    name = "home_bundle",
    srcs = ["//scripts:build-home-bundle.sh"],
    data = [":pack_home"],
    env = {"CLAX_PACK_HOME": "$(rootpath :pack_home)"},
)

# The macOS integration tests (`flutter test integration_test/<name>_test.dart
# -d macos`), a target per file, //apps/clax_app:integration_<name>: the
# debug app with the test as its entry point and the embedded clax, run in
# the logged-in session. They open the app's window and take minutes, so
# they are `manual`: `just app-integration` runs them.
[
    (
        integration_main(
            name = "_integration_%s_main" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            srcs = glob(["integration_test/*.dart"]),
            test = test,
            tags = ["manual"],
        ),
        flutter_application(
            name = "_integration_%s_app" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            package_name = "clax_app",
            srcs = glob(["lib/**/*.dart"]) + [":_integration_%s_main" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")]],
            assets = APP_ASSETS,
            main = ":_integration_%s_main.dart" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            tags = ["manual"],
            deps = [
                ":clax_app",
                "@clax_app_pub//:flutter_test",
                "@clax_app_pub//:integration_test",
                "@rules_flutter//flutter:material_icons",
            ],
        ),
        flutter_macos_app(
            name = "_integration_%s_macos" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            additional_contents = {":macos_clax": "Resources"},
            app_name = "clax_app",
            application = ":_integration_%s_app" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            bundle_id = "dev.empathic.clax",
            tags = ["manual"],
            version = ":macos_version",
        ),
        debug_app(
            name = "_integration_%s_debug" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            app = ":_integration_%s_macos" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            tags = ["manual"],
        ),
        sh_test(
            name = "integration_%s" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")],
            timeout = "long",
            srcs = ["tool/integration-run.sh"],
            args = ["$(rootpath :_integration_%s_debug)" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")]],
            data = [":_integration_%s_debug" % test[len("integration_test/"):-len("_test.dart")]],
            tags = [
                "exclusive",
                "manual",
                "no-remote",
                "no-sandbox",
            ],
            target_compatible_with = ["@platforms//os:macos"],
        ),
    )
    for test in glob(["integration_test/*_test.dart"])
]
